JavaScript Fetch API
In our useEffect hook, we can GET this course data and store it in our state. We will use the asynchronous Fetch API to get the information and store it. It is asynchronous because we don’t know how long it will take to get information from the server.

I strongly recommend that you read this page: MDN async await.

useEffect(() =&gt; {
